1
00:00:00,967 --> 00:00:02,033
<i>Do you know my daughter,
Joey Delgado?</i>

2
00:00:02,167 --> 00:00:04,100
<i>She said she would
wait for you here.</i>

3
00:00:04,233 --> 00:00:05,533
<i>She went over there,
to the market.</i>

4
00:00:05,667 --> 00:00:07,367
<i> The men who pushed me...</i>

5
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:08,633
<i> are there too.</i>

6
00:00:08,767 --> 00:00:10,767
<i>It looks like they're chasing
a student around here.</i>

7
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:12,267
<i> I even helped her escape...</i>

8
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,233
<i> from those ugly men.</i>

9
00:00:14,367 --> 00:00:15,367
<i> Where did she go?</i>

10
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:16,933
<i>There the one who is looking for
Miss Beautiful.</i>

11
00:00:17,067 --> 00:00:18,767
<i>Let's split up.
Go back there.</i>

12
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:20,133
<i> Got you!</i>

13
00:00:20,267 --> 00:00:22,233
<i>This is from that woman,
the one who bought from me.</i>

14
00:00:22,367 --> 00:00:23,567
<i>Where is she?
Tell me where she went!</i>

15
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:24,800
<i>Looks like the woman
already got away!</i>

16
00:00:24,933 --> 00:00:25,867
<i> Who are you?</i>

17
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:26,933
<i>Were you with the one
who shot my mommy?</i>

18
00:00:27,067 --> 00:00:28,667
<i>Did you come here
to finish the job?</i>

19
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,367
<i> That kid must've fooled us.</i>

20
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:32,467
<i>There she is!
- Hey, get in the car!</i>

21
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,833
<i>- Let's go!
- Hey!</i>

22
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,367
<i> Mr. Limjoco knows me.</i>

23
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:37,700
<i> What's going on here, Matias?</i>

24
00:00:37,833 --> 00:00:38,867
<i> You two know each other?</i>

25
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,433
<i>I'll explain everything to you.</i>

26
00:00:40,567 --> 00:00:42,500
<i>What do you need
with the woman you're chasing?</i>

27
00:00:42,633 --> 00:00:44,500
<i>Who are you? Are you her father?</i>

28
00:00:44,633 --> 00:00:45,567
<i> Joey...</i>

29
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:46,600
<i> You're safe now.</i>

30
00:00:46,733 --> 00:00:47,733
<i> My name is Jin Ho.</i>

31
00:00:47,867 --> 00:00:48,767
<i> You think I don't know?</i>

32
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,633
<i>You've been following me
since last night!</i>

33
00:00:51,367 --> 00:00:52,600
<i> Matias is my business partner.</i>

34
00:00:52,733 --> 00:00:54,200
<i> I'm sorry, Mr. Dizon.</i>

35
00:00:54,333 --> 00:00:55,933
<i>I wasn't really
going to shoot you.</i>

36
00:00:56,067 --> 00:00:56,900
<i> Just call me Andrew.</i>

37
00:00:57,033 --> 00:00:59,233
<i> I'm here on San Isidro Street.</i>

38
00:00:59,367 --> 00:01:00,567
<i> My stalker saved me.</i>

39
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:01,833
<i> What stalker?</i>

40
00:01:01,967 --> 00:01:03,600
<i> This is not my day.</i>

41
00:01:04,433 --> 00:01:06,467
<i> Hey, come back here!</i>

42
00:01:25,333 --> 00:01:26,300
Joey, what was that?

43
00:01:26,433 --> 00:01:27,833
<i> Dad, he left!</i>

44
00:01:27,967 --> 00:01:29,400
My stalker left!

45
00:01:29,533 --> 00:01:31,433
Where are you?
I'm coming to you.

46
00:01:31,567 --> 00:01:33,133
Dad, just meet me
at your boarding house.

47
00:01:33,267 --> 00:01:34,400
It's closer to you.

48
00:01:34,533 --> 00:01:36,633
<i>All right, I'll go home
right away after.</i>

49
00:01:36,767 --> 00:01:37,533
Oh, okay.

50
00:01:37,667 --> 00:01:39,067
Okay, Dad.

51
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:54,100
Hon...

52
00:01:54,233 --> 00:01:55,600
Where have you been?

53
00:01:55,733 --> 00:01:57,833
The guests were looking for you.

54
00:01:57,967 --> 00:02:00,800
And you, your nieces have been
looking for you too.

55
00:02:00,933 --> 00:02:03,133
Oh, I was just talking
to your sibling.

56
00:02:07,533 --> 00:02:09,567
What happened to you?
Why are you so dirty?

57
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:11,300
Even your back,
it's filthy.

58
00:02:11,433 --> 00:02:12,333
What happened to you?

59
00:02:12,467 --> 00:02:15,400
Oh, I must have
brushed against something.

60
00:02:15,567 --> 00:02:18,767
Oh, tell the kids
I'll make it up to them.

61
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:21,067
I just really,
really have to go.

62
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:22,767
Okay, sure.

63
00:02:23,833 --> 00:02:27,933
Brother, please take care
of sister and mom.

64
00:02:28,067 --> 00:02:29,433
Always.

65
00:02:30,433 --> 00:02:31,433
I'll go now.

66
00:02:31,567 --> 00:02:32,933
Okay.

67
00:02:33,067 --> 00:02:33,833
Take care.

68
00:02:33,967 --> 00:02:35,367
- Bye.
- Okay.

69
00:02:37,767 --> 00:02:40,167
Hon, I'll just talk to
the caterers, okay?

70
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:41,133
There's a small problem.

71
00:02:41,267 --> 00:02:43,000
- Okay.
- All right.

72
00:03:01,733 --> 00:03:03,300
Joey!

73
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:04,967
Why is that with you?
Where's Joey?

74
00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:06,333
Joey!

75
00:03:08,167 --> 00:03:09,967
What are you doing here?

76
00:03:10,667 --> 00:03:12,133
Oh...

77
00:03:12,267 --> 00:03:13,767
Why are you looking for Joey?

78
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:15,267
Did something happen?

79
00:03:17,667 --> 00:03:20,067
What happened to your face?
Did you get into a fight?

80
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:28,700
I'll just wait for Joey outside.

81
00:03:29,833 --> 00:03:31,633
Wait, Miguel!

82
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:36,467
You're not answering
my questions again.

83
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:39,267
Why are you so worried
about Joey?

84
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,900
Are you hiding something?

85
00:03:41,033 --> 00:03:43,800
I have no idea
what's going on anymore.

86
00:03:45,433 --> 00:03:47,767
If I tell you,
will you even believe me?

87
00:03:49,733 --> 00:03:52,000
Or will you believe Andrew Dizon

88
00:03:52,133 --> 00:03:54,300
more than your own husband?

89
00:03:54,467 --> 00:03:57,400
My husband doesn't even
talk to me.

90
00:03:58,767 --> 00:04:02,233
He always says
he's buried in work...

91
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:06,867
but it turns out
he's with another woman.

92
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:18,567
Sir.

93
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:21,167
Aren't you Major Miguel
Delgado's partner?

94
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,467
Yes, why?

95
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:25,100
I was hoping I could get
his contact number.

96
00:04:26,633 --> 00:04:27,867
Sir!

97
00:04:31,767 --> 00:04:32,900
The search warrant
has been issued.

98
00:04:33,033 --> 00:04:35,367
We're coordinating with the
Manila police force

99
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:37,767
to search Major Delgado's
belongings.

100
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:39,200
We expedited this

101
00:04:39,333 --> 00:04:42,200
because we don't want him
getting rid of any evidence

102
00:04:42,333 --> 00:04:44,533
connecting him to
Sergeant Orbos' death.

103
00:04:44,667 --> 00:04:45,567
Yes, Sir.

104
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:47,300
Follow me to the office.

105
00:05:04,733 --> 00:05:05,667
What are you doing?

106
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,200
You can't open my dad's car!

107
00:05:07,333 --> 00:05:09,233
What are you doing?

108
00:05:09,367 --> 00:05:10,600
Joey?

109
00:05:11,767 --> 00:05:13,133
That's Joey.
Joey.

110
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:16,267
- Sir, what is this?
- Joey?

111
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:18,100
Joey...

112
00:05:18,233 --> 00:05:19,800
- Joey...
- What's going on here?

113
00:05:19,933 --> 00:05:22,367
They want to open dad's car.

114
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:24,067
They're accusing him
of all sorts of things.

115
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:25,600
Miguel Delgado,
we have a warrant

116
00:05:25,733 --> 00:05:27,267
to search your vehicle.

117
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:29,267
Give us the key.

118
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:30,867
What?

119
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:39,567
Yes?

120
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,700
Sir, someone wants
to speak with you.

121
00:05:43,833 --> 00:05:45,000
It's Andrew Dizon.

122
00:05:45,133 --> 00:05:46,967
All right, let him in.

123
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:51,333
What do you need?

124
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:54,233
Oh...

125
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:57,867
Is it true that...

126
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Major Delgado
is the number one suspect

127
00:06:00,133 --> 00:06:01,733
in Orbos' murder?

128
00:06:01,867 --> 00:06:05,000
Oh right, you hate him.

129
00:06:05,133 --> 00:06:07,567
Not at all. I'm just curious...

130
00:06:07,733 --> 00:06:09,167
why Major Delgado...

131
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:11,133
is your number one suspect.

132
00:06:12,133 --> 00:06:14,100
What could be his motive?

133
00:06:14,233 --> 00:06:16,267
You know I can't tell you that,

134
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:18,533
the investigation is ongoing.

135
00:06:18,667 --> 00:06:22,067
But rest assured,
we're following protocol.

136
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:25,667
And we have strong reasons
for what we're doing.

137
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,967
This isn't easy for us either.

138
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:30,467
He's one of our own, after all.

139
00:06:31,267 --> 00:06:32,800
Wait, what warrant?

140
00:06:32,933 --> 00:06:34,633
What are you talking about?

141
00:06:34,767 --> 00:06:36,133
For what?

142
00:06:36,267 --> 00:06:38,133
Your husband is a suspect
in the death...

143
00:06:38,267 --> 00:06:40,900
of Staff Sergeant Ramon Orbos.

144
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:42,267
Miguel...

145
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:43,767
is this true?

146
00:06:45,667 --> 00:06:47,200
Are you doubting me?

147
00:06:47,333 --> 00:06:49,467
- Then what are they saying?
- Mom...

148
00:06:51,133 --> 00:06:52,800
What do you want me to do?

149
00:06:52,933 --> 00:06:54,467
Hand over the key?

150
00:06:55,367 --> 00:06:57,100
Here.

151
00:06:57,233 --> 00:06:58,733
Dad...

152
00:06:59,467 --> 00:07:00,833
If they don't find anything...

153
00:07:00,967 --> 00:07:02,333
- will you trust me?
- Search.

154
00:07:02,467 --> 00:07:05,200
Will you stop it!

155
00:07:05,333 --> 00:07:07,000
Dad, wait!

156
00:07:07,633 --> 00:07:09,500
You don't need to search
my dad's car...

157
00:07:09,633 --> 00:07:10,500
because I have proof...

158
00:07:10,633 --> 00:07:12,767
he's not the one
who killed Ramon Orbos!

159
00:07:15,833 --> 00:07:16,800
Wait.

160
00:07:16,933 --> 00:07:18,233
I can prove my dad is innocent.

161
00:07:18,367 --> 00:07:19,767
Wait.

162
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,500
Wait a second.
Wait, wait...

163
00:07:32,633 --> 00:07:34,067
Joey, what are you looking for?

164
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:35,900
Where is it?

165
00:07:36,033 --> 00:07:38,033
Wait!

166
00:07:38,167 --> 00:07:39,433
Where is it?

167
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:42,467
Peter knows!
Peter knows.

168
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:43,867
- Yes, it's true.
- We have proof.

169
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:46,433
Dad, this is what
I'm going to give you.

170
00:07:46,567 --> 00:07:47,733
This is the evidence...

171
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:49,200
that will clear your name.
Wait.

172
00:07:49,333 --> 00:07:50,833
It was really here.

173
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:53,300
Where is it?

174
00:08:00,933 --> 00:08:03,000
It's really gone.

175
00:08:03,133 --> 00:08:04,500
Excuse me.

176
00:08:05,733 --> 00:08:06,700
Where is it?

177
00:08:06,833 --> 00:08:07,800
- Joey...
- I put it here!

178
00:08:07,933 --> 00:08:09,433
Joey, what are you looking for?

179
00:08:09,567 --> 00:08:11,067
Mom, I put it...

180
00:08:12,033 --> 00:08:13,400
Joey...

181
00:08:15,733 --> 00:08:16,533
Dad, I'm sorry.

182
00:08:16,667 --> 00:08:19,000
I really put it here.

183
00:08:19,133 --> 00:08:20,367
I'm sorry.

184
00:08:21,467 --> 00:08:22,567
Dad, I'm sorry.

185
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:24,733
Joey...

186
00:08:24,867 --> 00:08:27,133
Don't talk to anyone.

187
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:29,433
The evidence you're holding...

188
00:08:29,567 --> 00:08:32,600
is the reason
they're chasing you.

189
00:08:32,733 --> 00:08:34,300
You weren't careful.

190
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:37,567
Andrew saw you...

191
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:40,300
and you even pulled out a gun.

192
00:08:41,233 --> 00:08:43,300
I held back, Boss.

193
00:08:43,433 --> 00:08:45,500
Your brother-in-law
just wouldn't stop.

194
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:48,300
You know me.

195
00:08:48,433 --> 00:08:50,300
I don't like being
at a disadvantage.

196
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:54,500
You're lucky he trusts me.

197
00:08:54,667 --> 00:08:58,067
Whatever I say, he believes.

198
00:08:58,833 --> 00:09:01,533
We really are business partners,
aren't we?

199
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:10,467
Is this registered, Major?

200
00:09:17,567 --> 00:09:19,000
Dad...

201
00:09:20,433 --> 00:09:21,533
What is that?

202
00:09:21,667 --> 00:09:23,433
Is that yours?

203
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:26,400
That gun isn't mine.

204
00:09:26,533 --> 00:09:28,500
I've only just seen it now.

205
00:09:34,133 --> 00:09:35,267
I only came...

206
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:38,900
because I knew you prefer
receiving good news in person.

207
00:09:40,233 --> 00:09:43,000
No one will block our operation
in Bolagos anymore.

208
00:09:44,233 --> 00:09:46,200
Parak already made sure...

209
00:09:46,333 --> 00:09:48,767
Delgado gets imprisoned.

210
00:09:56,567 --> 00:09:58,067
That gun doesn't belong to me.

211
00:09:58,200 --> 00:09:59,267
Just go to the precinct
and explain yourself there.

212
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:00,733
You'll be taken to Bolagos.

213
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:02,633
Wait a minute, I have evidence.

214
00:10:02,767 --> 00:10:05,367
You can't take my father!

215
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:07,233
Remember what I told you.

216
00:10:07,367 --> 00:10:09,767
I don't want you to get hurt,
Joey.

217
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:10,767
But, Dad...

218
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:12,167
I'll come with you.

219
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:13,000
Dad...

220
00:10:13,133 --> 00:10:14,567
Don't hurt my family.

221
00:10:15,833 --> 00:10:17,500
Dad , Dad , I have evidence.

222
00:10:17,633 --> 00:10:19,400
- I'll give it to you.
- Joey!

223
00:10:20,367 --> 00:10:21,867
Remember what I told you.

224
00:10:25,633 --> 00:10:26,633
Come with me.

225
00:10:26,767 --> 00:10:28,067
Dad, wait...

226
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,667
Dad...

227
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:31,567
Wait a minute, I have evidence.

228
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:32,933
Dad!

229
00:10:33,067 --> 00:10:34,433
I have evidence!

230
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,667
You can't take my father.

231
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:38,100
Dad!

232
00:10:39,133 --> 00:10:41,200
Peter, you know I have evidence,
right?

233
00:10:41,333 --> 00:10:42,433
- I have a video!
- Yes!

234
00:10:42,567 --> 00:10:44,833
He didn't kill Ramon Orbos!

235
00:10:44,967 --> 00:10:46,600
- Let's go, come on.
- Joey!

236
00:10:46,733 --> 00:10:48,267
Let's go.

237
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:50,133
Wait! Dad!

238
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:53,800
Mom, they can't take dad.

239
00:11:14,933 --> 00:11:16,867
Parak sent a message.

240
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,633
Delgado is on his way
to Bolagos.

241
00:11:23,267 --> 00:11:24,933
That's good to hear.

242
00:11:26,433 --> 00:11:29,233
We didn't make a mistake
in choosing Parak.

243
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:32,367
He's been very valuable to us.

244
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:34,500
Speaking of mistakes...

245
00:11:35,467 --> 00:11:38,067
There's something you need
to know about Lisa.

246
00:11:42,033 --> 00:11:44,100
She also has a problem?

247
00:11:44,233 --> 00:11:45,433
Someone intervened,

248
00:11:45,567 --> 00:11:47,700
that's why the woman
managed to escape.

249
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:51,267
And you still haven't
seen her face?

250
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:54,167
The hood of her red jacket
covered her face.

251
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:56,200
I was about to get closer,
Madam.

252
00:11:56,900 --> 00:11:58,800
I almost got her!

253
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:01,633
But suddenly a car arrived,

254
00:12:01,767 --> 00:12:04,700
and the woman got inside
the car.

255
00:12:04,833 --> 00:12:06,933
That's why I didn't catch her.

256
00:12:07,967 --> 00:12:09,567
Oh...

257
00:12:10,367 --> 00:12:12,133
Is that so?

258
00:12:16,567 --> 00:12:18,933
What's the use of your feet...

259
00:12:19,067 --> 00:12:20,833
if that's the case, huh?

260
00:12:23,167 --> 00:12:24,667
Oh, I'm sorry, Madam!

261
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:27,667
Madam!

262
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:29,267
Someone saw her...

263
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:31,733
while torturing Ramon,

264
00:12:31,867 --> 00:12:33,833
and they caught it on video.

265
00:12:36,367 --> 00:12:37,500
And?

266
00:12:41,933 --> 00:12:43,800
They're already working on...

267
00:12:45,167 --> 00:12:47,700
finding the witness...

268
00:12:47,867 --> 00:12:49,700
and getting the video.

269
00:12:50,933 --> 00:12:53,033
So far, no news yet.

270
00:12:55,367 --> 00:12:57,333
Call Lisa.

271
00:12:58,667 --> 00:13:00,267
Yes, Boss.

272
00:13:08,167 --> 00:13:10,033
That's enough! Ma'am!

273
00:13:17,633 --> 00:13:18,967
Hello?

274
00:13:21,533 --> 00:13:22,867
I'll be there.

275
00:13:26,233 --> 00:13:28,267
I'll call your Godfather Diego

276
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:29,667
to join us in Bolagos.

277
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:32,767
And maybe he can help.

278
00:13:33,833 --> 00:13:35,100
But Joey, I don't know

279
00:13:35,233 --> 00:13:37,667
how to deal
with your father now.

280
00:13:37,800 --> 00:13:38,867
What are you saying, Mom?

281
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:42,067
Do you really believe that
dad could do that?

282
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:43,633
Mom, dad is not a murderer,

283
00:13:43,767 --> 00:13:45,267
and that's not his gun!

284
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:47,567
I know all that!
He doesn't have any other gun!

285
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:49,567
Joey, my child...

286
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:51,433
Mom, didn't I tell you?

287
00:13:51,567 --> 00:13:52,600
I have proof!

288
00:13:52,733 --> 00:13:56,000
I have a video that will prove
that dad is innocent!

289
00:13:56,167 --> 00:13:58,867
I just can't find it right now,
but I do have a video!

290
00:14:02,333 --> 00:14:04,167
Joey, what are you going to do?

291
00:14:04,300 --> 00:14:06,967
I'll find the video,
I'll give it to dad.

292
00:14:07,100 --> 00:14:08,600
Joey!

293
00:14:09,967 --> 00:14:11,200
I'll help Joey.

294
00:14:11,333 --> 00:14:13,300
I'll talk to her.

295
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:55,500
Sir, Sir!
Can I ask for a statement?

296
00:14:55,633 --> 00:14:56,967
Did you kill
Sergeant Ramon Orbos?

297
00:14:57,100 --> 00:14:58,233
Sir! Sir! Are you part of...

298
00:14:58,367 --> 00:14:59,833
a drug trafficking syndicate?

299
00:14:59,967 --> 00:15:01,200
Sir, just give us an answer.
Sir?

300
00:15:01,367 --> 00:15:02,567
Did you kill
Sergeant Ramon Orbos?

301
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:04,867
Are you part of a drug
trafficking syndicate?

302
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,333
Sir, Sir, give us an answer,
Sir!

303
00:15:06,467 --> 00:15:07,400
Sir, did you kill him?

304
00:15:07,533 --> 00:15:09,100
Sir!

305
00:15:09,233 --> 00:15:10,267
Sir, Sir, Sir!

306
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:12,533
Sir, did you kill
Sergeant Ramon Orbos, Sir?

307
00:15:12,667 --> 00:15:14,000
Sir!

308
00:15:14,133 --> 00:15:16,133
Sir, give us a statement, Sir!

309
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,533
- Yes, Elai?
- Hello, Boss?

310
00:15:27,667 --> 00:15:29,067
They say Delgado
has been arrested.

311
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:31,767
I know, I'm here
at Bolagos Precinct.

312
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:33,000
Okay, good.
We'll follow there.

313
00:15:33,133 --> 00:15:34,500
That's where we're going
to do our livestream.

314
00:15:34,667 --> 00:15:37,100
No, no. Don't.

315
00:15:37,233 --> 00:15:39,233
There are a lot
of reporters here.

316
00:15:39,367 --> 00:15:42,167
<i>I want to tell the story
from a different angle.</i>

317
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:43,900
Anong angle?

318
00:16:09,867 --> 00:16:11,500
Joey, there's really nothing.

319
00:16:12,567 --> 00:16:14,633
What do you mean by nothing?
It's just there!

320
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:18,233
I'll take it from here!

321
00:16:20,867 --> 00:16:22,900
Just relax.
We'll find it, okay?

322
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,700
Joey...

323
00:16:27,833 --> 00:16:28,900
Ah, Mom, wait.

324
00:16:29,033 --> 00:16:30,200
I'll fix this later.

325
00:16:30,333 --> 00:16:32,567
I just need to find
the flash drive.

326
00:16:34,033 --> 00:16:35,833
Your Godfather is on his way.

327
00:16:37,433 --> 00:16:39,367
Mom, it's just right here.

328
00:16:40,233 --> 00:16:42,100
Joey...

329
00:16:42,267 --> 00:16:46,000
Joey, I know what your father
is going through is scary.

330
00:16:46,133 --> 00:16:48,067
But if he's not really guilty,

331
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:50,367
the truth will come out.

332
00:16:54,867 --> 00:16:56,267
Is this yours?

333
00:16:58,467 --> 00:17:01,400
Your father brought it
when he came here earlier.

334
00:17:01,533 --> 00:17:03,133
He saw it outside.

335
00:17:03,267 --> 00:17:05,467
Maybe it fell in your stuff.

336
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:08,700
In the market...

337
00:17:11,333 --> 00:17:13,033
What?

338
00:17:13,167 --> 00:17:14,400
Mom, I have to go back
to the market.

339
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:16,467
I think I left
the flash drive there.

340
00:17:16,633 --> 00:17:18,300
What about your godfather?

341
00:17:18,433 --> 00:17:19,733
I'll follow right away.

342
00:17:19,867 --> 00:17:20,833
When I get back, I'll have

343
00:17:20,967 --> 00:17:23,233
the evidence
that will free dad.

344
00:17:23,367 --> 00:17:24,433
Oh...

345
00:17:28,067 --> 00:17:30,767
Peter, let's go to the market.

346
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:32,100
Let's go.

347
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:35,167
Joey...

348
00:17:38,933 --> 00:17:41,633
The lab will analyze this gun.

349
00:17:41,767 --> 00:17:44,533
But so far,
this is the same caliber

350
00:17:44,667 --> 00:17:46,467
that killed Sergeant Orbos.

351
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:47,733
Sir, that gun is not mine.

352
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:49,867
Believe me.

353
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:53,167
I can't just take your word
for it, Major Delgado.

354
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:54,667
You know the process.

355
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:56,867
Sir, I know I've said
a lot of things,

356
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:59,033
but does it have
to come to this?

357
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:03,267
I don't like what you're
showing, Major Delgado!

358
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:05,433
This isn't personal.

359
00:18:05,567 --> 00:18:07,467
We're acting on the evidence...

360
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:09,067
found in your car!

361
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:10,467
Sir, I was set up.

362
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:12,567
That gun isn't mine.

363
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:14,833
Maybe it was planted
by those who arrested me.

364
00:18:14,967 --> 00:18:16,600
This guy is crazy!

365
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:20,567
Stop it, Major Delgado.

366
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:22,900
You're insulting our comrades.

367
00:18:23,067 --> 00:18:25,533
Cruz, take him in.

368
00:18:25,667 --> 00:18:26,400
Sir, I didn't kill Orbos.

369
00:18:26,533 --> 00:18:27,700
That's an order!

370
00:18:27,833 --> 00:18:29,100
Sir...

371
00:18:30,233 --> 00:18:32,333
Sir, I was set up!

372
00:18:38,733 --> 00:18:40,167
Are you sure about
what you're saying?

373
00:18:40,567 --> 00:18:42,033
Of course, Boss Idol.

374
00:18:42,167 --> 00:18:43,333
I heard it clearly.

375
00:18:43,467 --> 00:18:46,300
Chief said the gun
that killed Orbos...

376
00:18:46,433 --> 00:18:49,867
was found in
Major Delgado's car.

377
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,900
Oh, okay, Dante.
Thank you.

378
00:18:52,033 --> 00:18:54,200
Ah, okay, thank you very much
for this, too.

379
00:18:59,233 --> 00:19:00,633
Oh...

380
00:19:00,767 --> 00:19:03,967
It seems Delgado will no longer
get away with his crimes.

381
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:10,667
Do you really think
he killed Orbos?

382
00:19:10,800 --> 00:19:12,667
That's what the evidence says.

383
00:19:13,067 --> 00:19:15,633
But isn't it so convenient,
Elai...

384
00:19:16,633 --> 00:19:19,767
that the gun he used
to kill Orbos

385
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:21,667
is in his car?

386
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:23,600
It's been days.

387
00:19:23,733 --> 00:19:25,600
Why hasn't he
thrown it away yet?

388
00:19:26,533 --> 00:19:27,800
I don't know.
Maybe he's just stupid.

389
00:19:27,933 --> 00:19:29,433
He didn't think about it.

390
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:31,133
Elai, he's smart.

391
00:19:31,967 --> 00:19:35,033
He's not that stupid
to commit that mistake.

392
00:19:37,067 --> 00:19:40,033
Wait, are you saying
Delgado is innocent?

393
00:19:41,167 --> 00:19:44,300
Maybe you've forgotten,
it was you exposed him.

394
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:46,867
I know, I know...

395
00:19:47,967 --> 00:19:50,167
but at this point...

396
00:19:50,300 --> 00:19:51,900
my hunch is different.

397
00:19:53,533 --> 00:19:57,900
What if Major Delgado
was set up?

398
00:19:59,267 --> 00:20:00,867
Huh...

399
00:20:05,867 --> 00:20:08,233
You traitor!

400
00:20:08,367 --> 00:20:10,333
You should know by now...

401
00:20:10,467 --> 00:20:13,167
that Matias' loyalty is with me.

402
00:20:13,300 --> 00:20:16,500
So it's only right for him to
report your mistake.

403
00:20:16,633 --> 00:20:18,400
That wasn't a mistake.

404
00:20:18,533 --> 00:20:20,167
It was an accident.

405
00:20:20,300 --> 00:20:24,633
You were careless, that's why
someone took a video of you.

406
00:20:24,767 --> 00:20:27,600
Let me remind you, Lisa.

407
00:20:27,733 --> 00:20:30,233
I took you in to be
an asset in our operation.

408
00:20:30,367 --> 00:20:31,867
But if you'll be exposed,

409
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:33,167
you will become a liability.

410
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:35,467
That's not going to happen.

411
00:20:35,633 --> 00:20:36,800
That's why I'm doing
all I can...

412
00:20:36,933 --> 00:20:38,200
to find that girl...

413
00:20:38,333 --> 00:20:40,633
and get the video back.

414
00:20:40,767 --> 00:20:42,400
Make sure of it.

415
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:45,400
Boss, he's here.

416
00:20:46,833 --> 00:20:48,400
There he is.

417
00:20:48,867 --> 00:20:50,500
The man of the hour.

418
00:20:51,833 --> 00:20:53,533
Good job, Parak.

419
00:21:06,867 --> 00:21:08,600
Executioner.

420
00:21:26,667 --> 00:21:29,533
The first thing I destroyed
was Delgado's name.

421
00:21:29,667 --> 00:21:30,900
No one will believe him anymore.

422
00:21:31,033 --> 00:21:32,667
Did he really drive me away?

423
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:34,000
I was hurt too.

424
00:21:34,133 --> 00:21:35,833
I have evidence
that can help dad.

425
00:21:35,967 --> 00:21:36,800
I just need to find...

426
00:21:36,933 --> 00:21:37,867
that flash drive.

427
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:39,233
Flash drive?

428
00:21:39,367 --> 00:21:41,400
I'm doing something
to clear my name.

429
00:21:41,533 --> 00:21:43,633
I'm getting help from Boss Idol.

430
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:45,233
- You're so shameless!
- Hey, Joey, don't.

431
00:21:45,367 --> 00:21:46,567
Trust me.

432
00:21:46,700 --> 00:21:48,033
Never say die.

433
00:21:48,167 --> 00:21:49,600
Never say die.

434
00:21:49,733 --> 00:21:51,433
But she keeps telling me...

435
00:21:51,567 --> 00:21:53,200
she has proof.

436
00:21:53,333 --> 00:21:55,800
She'll prove Miguel's innocence.

437
00:21:55,933 --> 00:21:58,400
Someone saw her torturing Ramon.

438
00:21:58,533 --> 00:21:59,533
I can find it on my own.

439
00:21:59,667 --> 00:22:00,633
Can you really do it?

440
00:22:00,767 --> 00:22:03,633
I need her to tell me
where the video was taken.

441
00:22:03,767 --> 00:22:05,767
Don't worry, I'll find
Theresa very soon.

442
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:08,400
You were looking for evidence.

443
00:22:08,533 --> 00:22:09,900
It's a video.
